  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "footprint_mismatch",
      "components": ["C6"],
      "pins": ["C6.1", "C6.2"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(C6-Pad1)", "GND"],
      "observed": "C6 is a capacitor (value \"0.1uF\", libsource Device:C, description \"Unpolarized capacitor\") but its footprint is \"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\", an inductor land pattern. In addition, only pin 2 is attached (to GND); pin 1 sits on the floating net \"unconnected-(C6-Pad1)\".",
      "expected": "A capacitor should carry a capacitor footprint (e.g. C_0805_2012Metric...) and, as a decoupling/filter element, both terminals should be connected between a rail and GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"C6\") (value \"0.1uF\") (footprint \"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\")) ... (libsource (lib \"Device\") (part \"C\") (description \"Unpolarized capacitor\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"59\") (name \"unconnected-(C6-Pad1)\") (node (ref \"C6\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"},
        {"source": "spice", "quote": "C6 unconnected-_C6-Pad1_ 0 0.1u"}
      ],
      "impact": "C6 cannot perform any decoupling/filtering function because one terminal is open, so whatever node/rail it was meant to decouple loses its capacitor; the wrong (inductor) land pattern also risks wrong part placement/assembly.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    },
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["U11"],
      "pins": ["U11.13", "U11.14"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "SKW92A pins 13 and 14 (symbol function names LAN_PORT3_TX+ and LAN_PORT3_TX-) are both tied directly to the GND net, while the other PHY/GPIO pins are used for the keyboard/SD/EPD functions.",
      "expected": "Unused module pins should be left open or handled per the module's own pin-share guidance rather than shorted; shorting a differential transmit pair to ground is not standard practice.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX+\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"14\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX-\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"}
      ],
      "impact": "If the module's internal PHY still drives these pins, tying them to ground shorts the outputs (excess current/possible damage); otherwise the pins are simply held low. Either way they are unusable.",
      "confidence": 0.3
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The power, regulator, SKW92A, keyboard, microSD, EPD boost/inverter and load-switch sections all match the specification's stated connectivity and values, but C6 is a 0.1uF capacitor placed on an inductor land pattern with its pin 1 left floating (so it does nothing), and the SKW92A pins 13/14 are shorted to GND, so the build is not a clean copy of the intended design."
}

